  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations is vital for fostering strong, representative, and influential tripartite constituents, which is essential for effective social dialogue. This enhancement aligns with promoting development-oriented policies that support productive activities and decent job creation. By empowering these organizations, we can encourage entrepreneurship, creativity, and innovation while facilitating the formalization and growth of micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs). Access to financial services will further bolster these efforts, ensuring that employers&apos; organizations are independent and representative, ultimately contributing to a more dynamic and resilient economy that benefits all stakeholders in the labour market. The ILO in collaboration with the Fiji Chamber and Employers Federation (FCEF), co-designed a session at the Fiji Commerce and Employers Federation&#x2019;s Top Executive Conference (TOPEX). The session focused on addressing the high cost of doing business in Fiji, with particular emphasis on improving productivity, and streamlining the ease of doing business. It aimed to tackle critical challenges such as high labour costs, bureaucratic inefficiencies, and low productivity by exploring global best practices, sharing national insights, and identifying sustainable strategies for Fiji&apos;s economic growth. As part of the programme, ILO delivered a presentation titled Climate Change and Productivity, drawing on existing ILO publications and global good practices. The beneficiaries are the employers of Fiji and subsequently the workers of Fiji. ILO, also, in collaboration with FCEF conducted cross-sectoral employers&apos; survey on skills needs to develop an action plan for better alignment of skills development with private sector demand for skills.</narrative>
  </description>
